{"name":"Acid Blond","hex":"#efedd7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"acid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sour, sharp, or biting to the taste; tart; having the taste of vinegar.","Sour-tempered."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sour substance.","(chemistry)\nAny compound which yields H+ ions (protons) when dissolved in water; an Arrhenius acid.\n\nAny compound that easily donates protons to a base; a Brønsted acid.\nAny compound that can accept a pair of electrons to form a covalent bond; a Lewis acid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/acid"},{"term":"blond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bleached or pale golden (light yellowish) colour.","Particularly of a person, having blond hair."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pale yellowish (golden brown) color, especially said of hair color.","A person with this hair color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Acid","blocks":[{"text":"An acid is a molecule or ion capable of either donating a proton (i.e. hydrogen cation, H+), known as a Brønsted–Lowry acid, or forming a covalent bond with an electron pair, known as a Lewis acid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Zn_reaction_with_HCl.JPG/330px-Zn_reaction_with_HCl.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acid"},{"title":"Blond","blocks":[{"text":"Blond or blonde, also referred to as fair hair, is a human hair color characterized by low levels of eumelanin, the dark pigment. The resultant visible hue depends on various factors, but always has some yellowish color. The color can be from the very pale blond to reddish \"strawberry\" blond or golden-brownish (\"sandy\") blond colors. Occasionally, the state of being blond, and specifically the occurrence of blond traits in a predominantly dark or colored population are referred to as blondism.